# Packaging-tool noise, confirmed by locating each path inside the built
# backend image (see docs/phase9-ci-cd.md section 4): these dist-info
# METADATA entries live under setuptools/_vendor or pip/_vendor in the base
# image's bundled pip/setuptools/wheel. pip and setuptools are never invoked
# by the running app (CMD is `alembic upgrade head && uvicorn ...`), so these
# are unreachable at runtime, not a real finding against the app.
CVE-2026-23949
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-24049
# urllib3 2.7.0 here is pip's own vendored copy (pip/_vendor/urllib3) and
# botocore's legacy compat shim (botocore/vendored/requests/packages/
# urllib3), neither reachable at runtime. The real, top-level, importable
# urllib3 the app and botocore actually use is pinned >=2.8.0 in
# backend/requirements.txt (verified via `pip show urllib3` in the built
# image) and is NOT what these two IDs are flagging.
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

